    "source_record.json": {
      "background": "Collected from Oberwolfach Reports, which document mathematical workshops and their open-problem discussions.\n\n**Source report:** [Normal Families and Complex Dynamics (2007), Oberwolfach Reports, DOI 10.4171/owr/2007/09, pp. 487--548](https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2007/09)\n\n## Literature review (checked 2026-08-21)\n\n**Status:** partially solved\n\n**Assessment.** The condition is governed by boundary Schwarz--Pick and Julia--Caratheodory theory, which gives strong angular boundary conclusions and rigidity in extremal cases. A complete unrestricted description for every approach to the boundary point is not supplied by the standard theorem.\n\n**Sources checked.**\n\n- [original problem report](https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2007/09)\n- [Schwarz lemma at the boundary](https://arxiv.org/abs/1001.1805)\n- [hyperbolic distortion at the boundary](https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.13965)\n\nThis is a dated literature triage derived from the supplied OWR curation; verify time-sensitive status and cited claims independently.",
